Description:

A calendar's display name is no longer copied verbatim into the
Content-Disposition header of a CalDAV GET on the collection.  Control
characters and non-ASCII bytes now force RFC 8187 encoding, and a double
quote or backslash is escaped inside the quoted string as RFC 9110 requires.
Previously a display name holding a CRLF sequence truncated the header value
and allowed further headers to be added to the response, and one holding a
double quote or backslash could corrupt the header's parameters.  Separately,
httpd now drops any response header whose name or value holds a control
character other than HTAB, logging an error rather than emitting a corrupt
response.


